# Ex commands after :.

=== :s replaces the first match on the line
text:
|a a a
keys: :s/a/b/<CR>
want:
|b a a

=== :s with g replaces all
text:
|a a a
keys: :s/a/b/g<CR>
want:
|b b b

=== :%s on every line
text:
|foo 1
foo 2
bar foo
keys: :%s/foo/x/<CR>
want:
x 1
x 2
|bar x

=== groups and & in the replacement
text:
|john smith
keys: :s/\(\w\+\) \(\w\+\)/\2, \1 (&)/<CR>
want:
|smith, john (john smith)

=== case modifiers
text:
|hello world
keys: :s/\w\+/\u&/g<CR>
want:
|Hello World

=== \r inserts a line break
text:
|a,b
keys: :s/,/\r/<CR>
want:
a
|b

=== a range of lines
text:
|x
x
x
x
keys: :2,3s/x/y/<CR>
want:
x
y
|y
x

=== the visual lines as the range
text:
|a
a
a
keys: Vj:s/a/b/<CR>
want:
b
|b
a

=== a line number moves there
text:
|one
  two
three
keys: :2<CR>
want:
one
  |two
three

=== :d deletes lines
text:
|1
2
3
keys: :2,3d<CR>
want:
|1

=== an unknown command is an error
text:
|x
keys: :nosuch<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes

=== :s without a match is an error
text:
|x
keys: :s/zzz/y/<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes

=== :noh and :set keep the text
text:
|x
keys: :set ic<CR>:noh<CR>
want:
|x

=== ignorecase set by :set
text:
|a FOO
keys: :set ic<CR>/foo<CR>
want:
a |FOO

=== Esc cancels the command line
text:
|abc
keys: :s/a/b/<Esc>
want:
|abc
mode: vim/normal

=== :w writes the file
text:
|abc
keys: xx:w<CR>
want:
|c

=== marks give a range
text:
|1
2
3
4
keys: jmajmbgg:'a,'bd<CR>
want:
1
|4

=== a pattern gives a range: the next line it matches
text:
|1
foo
3
foo
keys: :/foo/d<CR>
want:
1
|3
foo

=== a backward pattern and the cursor's line
text:
1
foo
3
|4
keys: :?foo?,.d<CR>
want:
|1

=== :s runs what follows a | after its flags
text:
|a
a
x
keys: :2,3s/a/b/ | 1d<CR>
want:
|b
x

=== a | in the pattern of :s is the character
text:
|a|b
keys: :s/a|b/x/<CR>
want:
|x

=== a range on a command that takes none is an error
text:
|x
keys: :5w<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes

=== ranges alone after a |
text:
|1
2
3
keys: :3 | 2<CR>
want:
1
|2
3

=== a line starting with another character is not a command
text:
|x
keys: :!x<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes
